IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art26-demand`

-- g8-art27-28-required-steps: Articles 27 and 28 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice, the power to serve it,
-- the Minister's power to make an Order on procedure, the Minister's power to categorize organized religious charities, and the invalidity of a notice to the extent that it
-- requires an organized religious charity or its governor to suspend, remove or replace a governor.
-- The Commissioner's belief, the Commissioner's opinion that steps are appropriate, the Minister's appearance and the content of every Order are inputs.
-- Facts that other groups decide arrive as GIVENs under the standard names of PLAN section (c); this module never calls another group.
-- The time a notice specifies (27(2)) is counted as in Article 26(1): `Art 26(1) the last day allowed by the notice` (fork F8.7) is used here too.

§ `Part 7 -- Information and enforcement`

§§ `Article 27 -- Required steps notices`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 27(1): the five beliefs that prompt a notice
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `27(1) -- paragraph (2) applies if the Commissioner believes ...`

-- F8.14.  The Law says "if the Commissioner believes that".  Reading A (taken): the belief alone is the ground; whether it is right is for an appeal (34(1): wrong or unreasonable on the facts).
-- Reading B: the belief must also be borne out by the facts the other groups decide (IP8, IP12, IP14, IP15, IP16, IP21).  Under both readings nothing is a ground unless the entity is
-- a registered charity: every limb speaks of "a registered charity".
-- src:640 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies if the Commissioner believes that –
-- src:641 | (a) there has been misconduct by a registered charity;
-- src:642 | (b) a registered charity does not pass the charity test;
-- src:643 | (c) a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct;
-- src:644 | (d) a governor of a registered charity is, by reason of a reportable matter, unfit to be a governor of a registered charity; or
-- src:645 | (e) a registered charity has ceased to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d).
@ref Article 27(1)(a) (src:641)
GIVEN belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief the Commissioner holds
      `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP12: whether the conduct of the registered charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the entity meets the charity test
      `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP14: whether a governor of the registered charity has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc IP5: the entity as Article 2 leaves it; each governor carries the reportable matters that describe the person (IP21)
      `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that a governor of the registered charity is, by reason of a reportable matter, unfit to be a governor of a registered charity (Article 27(1)(d)); a judgement the caller supplies
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP15
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP16
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(1) the belief is borne out` belief `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the entity meets the charity test` `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)` `the entity` `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER belief
    WHEN `there has been misconduct by a registered charity` THEN `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
    WHEN `a registered charity does not pass the charity test` THEN NOT `the entity meets the charity test`
    WHEN `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct` THEN `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)`
    WHEN `a governor of a registered charity is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` THEN
            `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter`
        AND any (GIVEN g YIELD NOT null (g's `reportable matters`)) (`the entity`'s governors)
    WHEN `a registered charity has ceased to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` THEN
            NOT `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met`
        OR  NOT `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met`

@ref Article 27(1) (src:640-645)
@export Which of the five beliefs of Article 27(1) give the Commissioner a ground to serve a required steps notice: the beliefs held, if the entity is a registered charity (default - the belief alone is the ground); with the other reading, only those the facts bear out
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.14 is the one read here)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6: whether the entity is a registered charity (general or restricted section)
      `the Commissioner's beliefs` IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The beliefs among the five of Article 27(1) that the Commissioner holds; the Commissioner's belief is an input
      `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP12: whether the conduct of the registered charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the entity meets the charity test
      `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP14: whether a governor of the registered charity has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc IP5: the entity as Article 2 leaves it; each governor carries the reportable matters that describe the person (IP21)
      `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The determination that a governor of the registered charity is, by reason of a reportable matter, unfit to be a governor of a registered charity (Article 27(1)(d)); a judgement the caller supplies
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP15
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP16
GIVETH A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice`
`Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the Commissioner's beliefs` `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the entity meets the charity test` `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)` `the entity` `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the entity is a registered charity`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `what Article 27(1) requires of the Commissioner's belief`
         WHEN `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)` THEN `the Commissioner's beliefs`
         WHEN `the Commissioner's belief must also be borne out under Article 27(1)` THEN
              filter (GIVEN b YIELD `Art 27(1) the belief is borne out` b `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` `the entity meets the charity test` `the governor has engaged in misconduct within Article 18(4)` `the entity` `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met`) `the Commissioner's beliefs`

@ref Article 27(1) (src:640-645)
GIVEN grounds IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The beliefs that are grounds, from Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` grounds MEANS
    NOT null grounds

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 27(3): the relevant persons
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `27(3) -- the relevant persons`

-- src:647 | (3) The relevant persons for the purpose of paragraph (2) are –
-- src:648 | (a) the registered charity; and
-- src:649 | (b) the governors of the registered charity.
@ref Article 27(3) (src:647-649)
GIVEN `the person is the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 27(3)(a)
      `the person is a governor of the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 27(3)(b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(3) the person is a relevant person` `the person is the registered charity` `the person is a governor of the registered charity` MEANS
        `the person is the registered charity`
    OR  `the person is a governor of the registered charity`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 27(2): the power to serve the notice
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `27(2) -- the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice`

-- The power is a permission of the Commissioner, available when one of the beliefs of 27(1) is a ground, the notice specifies steps and a time, the Commissioner is of the opinion that the
-- steps are appropriate to remedy the matter, and the procedure and restrictions of any Order under 27(5) are met.  Opinion and Order are inputs.  The recipient must be a relevant person (27(3));
-- the notice may go to "any one or more", so each service is its own use of the power.
-- src:646 | (2) The Commissioner may serve written notice on any one or more of the relevant persons, within the meaning of paragraph (3), requiring steps specified in the notice to be taken by that person in a time specified in the notice, being steps that in Commissioner’s opinion are appropriate to remedy the matter prompting service of the notice.
@ref Article 27(2) (src:646)
@export Whether the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice on a relevant person: one of the beliefs of Article 27(1) is a ground, the notice specifies steps and a time, the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter, and any Order under Article 27(5) is met; FULFILLED where one of those fails
GIVEN grounds IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The beliefs that are grounds, from Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice
      belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief on which this notice would be served
      `the person is a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to be served is a relevant person under Article 27(3)
      `the notice specifies the steps and a time for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 27(2): the notice requires steps specified in it to be taken in a time specified in it
      `the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Commissioner's opinion is a judgement the caller supplies
      `the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE where no Order has been made under Article 27(5); otherwise whether its procedure and restrictions are met (the content of the Order is an input)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 27(2) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` grounds belief `the person is a relevant person` `the notice specifies the steps and a time for them` `the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter` `the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met` MEANS
    IF       elem belief grounds
         AND `the person is a relevant person`
         AND `the notice specifies the steps and a time for them`
         AND `the steps are in the Commissioner's opinion appropriate to remedy the matter`
         AND `the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `serve a required steps notice`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- IP27.  The decision whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice is likewise a decision of the Commissioner that Article 33(3) lets the person served appeal.
@ref Article 27(2) (src:646)
@export The decision of the Commissioner whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice, as the decision that Article 33(3) lets the person served appeal: imposed is 'the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed', not imposed is 'the Commissioner refuses'
GIVEN `the Commissioner imposes the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner decided to impose the requirement contained in the notice
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`Art 27 the decision of the Commissioner to impose a requirement` `the Commissioner imposes the requirement` MEANS
    `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH
        subject IS `whether to impose a requirement contained in a required steps notice`
        outcome IS (IF `the Commissioner imposes the requirement` THEN `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed` ELSE `the Commissioner refuses`)

-- IP19.  Each service of a notice is a record, which G1, G3 and G6 take as an input.  The time the notice specifies is counted as in Article 26(1) (F8.7).
-- `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` records what the notice PURPORTS to require; the invalidity of Article 28(3) is applied separately, by `Art 28(3)`.
@ref Article 27(2) (src:646)
@export The record of one service of a required steps notice, for the other groups: whom it was served on, the belief it rests on, the day it was served, the last day for the steps (counted as the reading of F8.7 says) and whether it purports to require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.7 is the one read here)
      recipient IS A `Recipient of a required steps notice` @desc Whom the notice was served on: the registered charity or a governor of it
      belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief on which the notice was served
      `the date on which the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc IP34: the day on which the notice was served
      spec IS A `Time specified in a notice` @desc The time the notice specifies for the steps: a date, or a number of days after the day of service
      requirements IS A LIST OF `Requirement in a required steps notice` @desc The requirements the notice contains
      `the steps required have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the steps required have been taken
GIVETH A `Required steps notice`
`Art 27(2) the required steps notice served` interp recipient belief `the date on which the notice was served` spec requirements `the steps required have been taken` MEANS
    `Required steps notice` WITH
        `served on` IS recipient
        `prompted by` IS belief
        `date served` IS `the date on which the notice was served`
        `steps to be taken by` IS JUST (`Art 26(1) the last day allowed by the notice` interp spec `the date on which the notice was served`)
        `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS any (GIVEN r YIELD `Art 27(4) the requirement is to suspend, remove or replace a governor` r) requirements
        `has been complied with` IS `the steps required have been taken`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 27(4): suspension, removal or replacement of a governor
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `27(4) -- the steps may include the suspension, removal or replacement of a governor`

-- src:650 | (4) If the notice is served by virtue of paragraph (1)(c) or (d), the steps required may include (subject to Article 28) the suspension, removal or replacement of the governor referred to in that paragraph.
@ref Article 27(4) (src:650)
GIVEN requirement IS A `Requirement in a required steps notice` @desc One requirement of a notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) the requirement is to suspend, remove or replace a governor` requirement MEANS
        requirement's `kind of requirement` EQUALS `a requirement to suspend a governor`
    OR  requirement's `kind of requirement` EQUALS `a requirement to remove a governor`
    OR  requirement's `kind of requirement` EQUALS `a requirement to replace a governor`

-- F8.15.  "If the notice is served by virtue of paragraph (1)(c) or (d), the steps required may include (subject to Article 28) the suspension, removal or replacement of the governor referred to
-- in that paragraph."  Reading A (taken): only a notice under (1)(c) or (d), because only those paragraphs refer to a governor.  Reading B: 27(4) only confirms what 27(2) already allows, so a notice
-- on any ground may.  Under both, "subject to Article 28": an organized religious charity (or its governor) may not be required to, because Article 28(3) voids the requirement (IP20).
@ref Article 27(4) (src:650)
GIVEN belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief on which the notice is served
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) reading A: the belief is one under Article 27(1)(c) or (d)` belief MEANS
        belief EQUALS `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`
    OR  belief EQUALS `a governor of a registered charity is unfit by reason of a reportable matter`

@ref Article 27(4) (src:650)
@export Whether the steps a required steps notice requires may include the suspension, removal or replacement of a governor: only for a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) (default), and never where the charity is an organized religious charity (Article 28(3))
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.15 is the one read here)
      belief IS A `Belief that prompts a required steps notice` @desc The belief on which the notice is served
      `the entity is an organized religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP20: whether the charity is an organized religious charity (see Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` interp belief `the entity is an organized religious charity` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is an organized religious charity`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER interp's `which notices may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`
         WHEN `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` THEN `Art 27(4) reading A: the belief is one under Article 27(1)(c) or (d)` belief
         WHEN `a notice on any ground in Article 27(1) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` THEN TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 27(5): the Minister's Order
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `27(5) -- the Minister may make further provision by Order`

-- src:651 | (5) The Minister may by Order make further provision as to the procedure for, and restrictions on, serving a notice under this Article.
@ref Article 27(5) (src:651)
@export The Minister's power to make an Order on the procedure for, and restrictions on, serving a required steps notice; the content of the Order is an input and is read by Art 27(2) as 'the procedure and restrictions of any Order under Article 27(5) are met'
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 27(5) the Minister may by Order make further provision` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order on the procedure for and restrictions on serving a required steps notice`

§§ `Article 28 -- Required steps notices restricted in relation to governors of organized religious charities`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 28(1): the Minister's power to categorize
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `28(1) -- the Minister may by Order provide for registered charities to be categorized`

-- F8.3.  (a) asks whether the charity meets the charity test "by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)", "whether solely or in combination with any other charitable purpose".  Article 6(2)(f) makes the advancement of
-- a philosophical belief analogous to (c) and so a purpose within (p), not (c) (T27).  Reading A (taken): only a purpose within (c) itself (IP11).  Reading B: a philosophical belief purpose counts too.
-- Both limbs are things that "appear to the Minister".  (a) has a computable core, the facts the Minister's appearance is formed from; (b) has none, and is an input.
-- src:653 | (1) The Minister may by Order provide for registered charities to be categorized as organized religious charities for the purpose of paragraph (3), being registered charities that appear to the Minister –
-- src:654 | (a) to meet the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c), whether solely or in combination with any other charitable purpose; and
-- src:655 | (b) to be organized in such a way that the supervision and discipline of the governors of the registered charity, in relation to the activities of the registered charity in Jersey (whether or not also in relation to activities elsewhere), is adequate to justify the application of paragraph (3).
@ref Article 28(1)(a) (src:654)
GIVEN `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the charity meets the charity test
      `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP11: whether the charity has a purpose that falls within Article 6(1)(c) itself, not merely analogous under 6(2)(f)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1)(a) reading A: meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` MEANS
        `the entity meets the charity test`
    AND `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)`

@ref Article 28(1)(a) (src:654)
GIVEN `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the charity meets the charity test
      `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP11
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc IP5: the entity; its purposes record which advance a philosophical belief (Article 6(2)(f))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1)(a) reading B: meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c) or an analogous philosophical belief purpose` `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity` MEANS
        `the entity meets the charity test`
    AND (   `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)`
         OR any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `is advancing a philosophical belief`) (`the entity`'s purposes) )

@ref Article 28(1)(a) (src:654)
@export Whether the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c), whether solely or with other purposes (default - only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts; with the other reading a philosophical belief purpose counts too)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.3 is the one read here)
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the charity meets the charity test
      `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP11: whether the charity has a purpose that falls within Article 6(1)(c) itself, not merely analogous under 6(2)(f)
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc IP5: the entity; its purposes record which advance a philosophical belief (Article 6(2)(f))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` interp `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether Article 28(1)(a) reaches a philosophical belief purpose`
    WHEN `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)` THEN `Art 28(1)(a) reading A: meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)`
    WHEN `a philosophical belief purpose also counts under Article 28(1)(a)` THEN `Art 28(1)(a) reading B: meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c) or an analogous philosophical belief purpose` `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity`

@ref Article 28(1)(b) (src:655)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Minister's appearance is an input; whether or not the charity is also supervised in relation to activities elsewhere is irrelevant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1)(b) the supervision and discipline of the governors is adequate to justify Article 28(3)` `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate` MEANS
    `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate`

@ref Article 28(1) (src:653-655)
@export Whether a registered charity is one an Order under Article 28(1) may categorize as an organized religious charity: it meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c), and it appears to the Minister that its governors are adequately supervised and disciplined in respect of its Jersey activities
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36 (F8.3 is the one read here)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6: whether the entity is a registered charity
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP8: whether the charity meets the charity test
      `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP11
      `the entity` IS AN Entity @desc IP5: the entity
      `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 28(1)(b): the Minister's appearance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity` `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate` MEANS
        `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` interp `the entity meets the charity test` `the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c)` `the entity`
    AND `Art 28(1)(b) the supervision and discipline of the governors is adequate to justify Article 28(3)` `it appears to the Minister that the charity is organized so that the supervision and discipline of its governors in respect of its activities in Jersey is adequate`

@ref Article 28(1) (src:653-655)
@export The Minister's power to provide by Order for a registered charity to be categorized as an organized religious charity: available only for a charity that is eligible; FULFILLED where it is not
GIVEN `the charity is eligible to be categorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The result of Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 28(1) the Minister may by Order provide for the charity to be categorized` `the charity is eligible to be categorized` MEANS
    IF   `the charity is eligible to be categorized`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `make an Order categorizing registered charities as organized religious charities`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 28(2): what the Order may contain
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `28(2) -- the provision that may be made`

-- src:656 | (2) The provision that may be made under paragraph (1) includes, without limitation –
-- src:657 | (a) provision granting discretion to the Commissioner to grant or withdraw status as an organized religious charity;
@ref Article 28(2)(a) (src:657)
@export The Commissioner's power to grant or withdraw status as an organized religious charity, where an Order under Article 28(1) gives that discretion; FULFILLED where it does not
GIVEN `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 28(2)(a): the content of the Order is an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 26 to 31`
`Art 28(2)(a) the Commissioner may grant or withdraw the status` `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` MEANS
    IF   `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY `grant or withdraw status as an organized religious charity`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- IP20.  A charity is an organized religious charity when it is a registered charity that an Order categorizes, or (where the Order gives the Commissioner the discretion) that the Commissioner has
-- granted the status, and the Commissioner has not withdrawn it.  Whether the Order was within the Minister's power is Art 28(1) the charity is eligible; it is not re-asked here, because "appear to the
-- Minister" is the Minister's judgement and the Order is an input.
@ref Article 28(1) and (2)(a) (src:653-657)
@export Whether a charity is an organized religious charity: it is a registered charity that an Order under Article 28 categorizes as one or (where the Order gives the discretion) that the Commissioner has granted the status to, and the Commissioner has not withdrawn the status
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP6: whether the entity is a registered charity
      order IS AN `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` @desc What the Order says about this charity, and what the Commissioner has done under any discretion the Order gives
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` `the entity is a registered charity` order MEANS
        `the entity is a registered charity`
    AND (   order's `the Order categorizes the charity as an organized religious charity`
         OR (    order's `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status`
             AND order's `the Commissioner has granted the status` ))
    AND NOT (    order's `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status`
             AND order's `the Commissioner has withdrawn the status` )

-- 28(2)(b), (i), (ii) and (iii): inert.  They name three statuses on which an Order may distinguish between charities.  The Scottish and UK Acts they cite are not among the sources, and what an
-- Order does with the statuses is the Order's content, an input; no rule of this encoding reads them.
-- src:658 | (b) provision that distinguishes between charities on the basis of the status of the charity as –
-- src:659 | (i) a designated religious charity within the meaning of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 of the Scottish Parliament,
-- src:660 | (ii) an institution falling within section 10(2) of the Charities Act 2011 of the parliament of the United Kingdom, or
-- src:661 | (iii) an entity in Jersey that is similar to such a designated religious charity or to such an institution.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 28(3): invalidity to the extent
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `28(3) -- a notice is invalid to the extent that it requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`

-- The notice is served on the charity or on a governor of it (the relevant persons of 27(3)), so for the charity the notice concerns the recipient is always within the Article.
-- It is invalid "to the extent that" it requires a governor OF THAT CHARITY to be suspended, removed or replaced: the other requirements of the notice stand.
-- src:662 | (3) A required steps notice served on an organized religious charity, or on a governor of such a charity, is invalid to the extent that it purports to impose a requirement to suspend, remove or replace a governor of that charity.
@ref Article 28(3) (src:662)
@export Whether one requirement of a required steps notice is invalid under Article 28(3): the charity is an organized religious charity and the requirement is to suspend, remove or replace a governor of that charity
GIVEN `the entity is an organized religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP20: whether the charity the notice concerns is an organized religious charity
      requirement IS A `Requirement in a required steps notice` @desc One requirement of the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` `the entity is an organized religious charity` requirement MEANS
        `the entity is an organized religious charity`
    AND `Art 27(4) the requirement is to suspend, remove or replace a governor` requirement
    AND requirement's `the governor concerned is a governor of the charity`

@ref Article 28(3) (src:662)
@export The requirements of a required steps notice that remain valid after Article 28(3): all of them unless the charity is an organized religious charity, and then all but those requiring a governor of that charity to be suspended, removed or replaced
GIVEN `the entity is an organized religious charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP20: whether the charity the notice concerns is an organized religious charity
      requirements IS A LIST OF `Requirement in a required steps notice` @desc The requirements the notice contains
GIVETH A LIST OF `Requirement in a required steps notice`
`Art 28(3) the requirements of the notice that remain valid` `the entity is an organized religious charity` requirements MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` `the entity is an organized religious charity` r) requirements
